EXPERIMENT 38 – CORRELATING DYNAMIC VALUES USING JSON EXTRACTOR IN APACHE JMETER
AIM
To use Apache JMeter to correlate dynamic values using the JSON Extractor.
ALGORITHM
1. Start Apache JMeter and rename the Test Plan.
2. Add a Thread Group under Test Plan.
3. Set Number of Threads = 3, Ramp-up Period = 3 seconds and Loop Count = 1.
4. Add an HTTP Request with method GET and path /uuid to generate a random ID in the JSON response.
5. Add Post Processors → JSON Extractor to the first sampler.
6. Extract the value using JSON Path $.uuid into the variable uid.
7. Add a second HTTP Request with path /anything/${uid}.
8. Add a Response Assertion with pattern ${uid}.
9. Add View Results Tree, run the plan and verify that the extracted ID is used in the second request.
INPUT – TEST PLAN CONFIGURATION
Element	Property	Value
Thread Group	Number of Threads	3
Thread Group	Ramp-up Period	3 seconds
Thread Group	Loop Count	1
HTTP Request 1	Protocol / Server	https / httpbin.org
HTTP Request 1	Method / Path	GET /uuid
JSON Extractor	Variable Name	uid
JSON Extractor	JSON Path	$.uuid
JSON Extractor	Match No.	1
JSON Extractor	Default Value	NOT_FOUND
HTTP Request 2	Method / Path	GET /anything/$
Response Assertion	Pattern	${uid}

OUTPUT
View Results Tree
Request 1 : GET https://httpbin.org/uuid
            -> {"uuid": "<random-id>"}

Request 2 : GET https://httpbin.org/anything/<random-id>
            -> Response code 200

Response Assertion : Passed


Summary Report
Metric	Value
Total Samples	6
Error %	0.00%

RESULT
Thus, Apache JMeter was used to correlate dynamic values using the JSON Extractor and the results were verified.
